  "content": {
    "id": "p9-q2-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "2",
    "prompt": "Consider the sample space $\\Omega=\\{1,2,3,\\ldots,60\\}$ and events\n$$\\begin{aligned}A&=\\{2,4,6,\\ldots,60\\},\\\\B&=\\{3,6,9,\\ldots,60\\}.\\end{aligned}$$\nAn element from $\\Omega$ is chosen at random. Find:",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p9-q2-first-six",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "",
        "prompt": "",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 2,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p9-q2-a",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "a",
            "prompt": "$\\Pr(A)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac12$",
              "worked": "There are $30$ even numbers in $\\Omega$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(A)&=\\frac{30}{60}\\\\\\Pr(A)&=\\frac12.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          },
          {
            "id": "p9-q2-b",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "b",
            "prompt": "$\\Pr(B')$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac23$",
              "worked": "There are $20$ multiples of $3$ in $\\Omega$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(B')&=1-\\Pr(B)\\\\\\Pr(B')&=1-\\frac{20}{60}\\\\\\Pr(B')&=\\frac23.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 24
          },
          {
            "id": "p9-q2-c",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "c",
            "prompt": "$\\Pr(A\\cap B)$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac16$",
              "worked": "$A\\cap B$ contains the multiples of $6$. There are $10$ of these in $\\Omega$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(A\\cap B)&=\\frac{10}{60}\\\\\\Pr(A\\cap B)&=\\frac16.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 20
          },
          {
            "id": "p9-q2-d",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "d",
            "prompt": "$\\Pr(A\\cap B')$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac13$",
              "worked": "Of the $30$ even numbers, $10$ are multiples of $3$. Thus $A\\cap B'$ contains $20$ outcomes.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(A\\cap B')&=\\frac{30-10}{60}\\\\\\Pr(A\\cap B')&=\\frac{20}{60}\\\\\\Pr(A\\cap B')&=\\frac13.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 24
          },
          {
            "id": "p9-q2-e",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "e",
            "prompt": "$\\Pr(A'\\cup B')$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac56$",
              "worked": "$A'\\cup B'$ contains every outcome except those in both $A$ and $B$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(A'\\cup B')&=1-\\Pr(A\\cap B)\\\\\\Pr(A'\\cup B')&=1-\\frac16\\\\\\Pr(A'\\cup B')&=\\frac56.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 26
          },
          {
            "id": "p9-q2-f",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "f",
            "prompt": "$\\Pr(A'\\cap B')$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac13$",
              "worked": "$A'\\cap B'$ contains outcomes in neither $A$ nor $B$.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr(A\\cup B)&=\\frac{30}{60}+\\frac{20}{60}-\\frac{10}{60}\\\\\\Pr(A\\cup B)&=\\frac23.\\\\\\Pr(A'\\cap B')&=1-\\Pr(A\\cup B)\\\\\\Pr(A'\\cap B')&=1-\\frac23\\\\\\Pr(A'\\cap B')&=\\frac13.\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 32
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p9-q2-i",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "i",
        "prompt": "$\\Pr\\big((A\\cap B')\\cup(B\\cap A')\\big)$",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p9-q2-i-short-result",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "\\frac12",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p9-q2-i-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": "Add the probabilities of the two disjoint regions belonging to exactly one event.",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "$A\\cap B'$ contains $30-10=20$ outcomes, and $B\\cap A'$ contains $20-10=10$ outcomes. These events are disjoint.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\Pr\\big((A\\cap B')\\cup(B\\cap A')\\big)&=\\frac{20}{60}+\\frac{10}{60}\\\\\\Pr\\big((A\\cap B')\\cup(B\\cap A')\\big)&=\\frac12.\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 28
      }
    ]
  },
